---
// The bundle's typed relations, drawn from knowledge/graph.json, and on a
// domain host the workspace's, drawn from the graph.json the federation
// workflow serves beside the site, which scripts/sync.mjs names in
// src/generated/workspace.json.
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";
import KnowledgeGraph from "../components/KnowledgeGraph.astro";
import workspace from "../generated/workspace.json";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: "Knowledge graph",
    description: "Every concept in the knowledge bundle and the typed relations between them.",
    tableOfContents: false,
  }}
>
  <p>
    Each node is a concept in the <a href={`${base}/knowledge/`}>knowledge bundle</a>, and each edge
    is a typed relation from a concept's frontmatter, such as <code>about</code>,
    <code>derivedFrom</code> or <code>relatedTo</code>, under the RDF predicate it projects to. A link
    written in a concept's body is not an edge. Search dims the nodes that do not match, the boxes
    hide node types and predicates, and selecting a node shows its details and a link to its page.
    The page's address names the selected concept, so a link to it opens the graph there.
  </p>
  <p>
    The trust shown in a node's details is the toolkit's tier. A concept's page gives its label in
    the words the curator and the docent use. The same graph is{" "}
    <a href={`${base}/knowledge/graph.nt`}>graph.nt</a> as N-Triples and{" "}
    <a href={`${base}/knowledge/concepts.jsonld`}>concepts.jsonld</a> as JSON-LD.
  </p>
  {
    workspace && (
      <p>
        This repository is a domain. The workspace view draws every bundle its members name, each in
        a colour of its own, with the links between bundles dashed. Each node links to its IRI, which
        a bundle with a site of its own serves as the concept's page. The view reads{" "}
        <a href={workspace.index}>the workspace</a> the newest release built, which the federation
        workflow adds to the site after building it.
      </p>
    )
  }
  <KnowledgeGraph workspace={workspace?.graph} />
</StarlightPage>
